{"id": "EUVD-2026-103770", "enisaUuid": "c5a42af6-3955-3ef4-94b1-e94130335f68", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: wfx: validate MIB read length before copying to caller\n\nwfx_hif_read_mib() copies reply->length bytes from the firmware\nresponse into the caller-provided buffer without checking that\nreply->length does not exceed val_len. A firmware response with\na length field larger than expected overruns the caller buffer and\nreads past the end of the reply allocation.\n\nReplace the dead -ENOMEM check with an active validation that\nreply->length fits within val_len before the memcpy.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/819d4c1323e2a9b7329021d5367aa01add22b5dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/02886c18a340da59df57365f29009e1258bfe333", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71d140099165de03128c00dd129f1eab21c6a3c4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7acb36fd60a3e7b858f12e69a919c3609b281408", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce67ebe9d8629776ce38e6995ae72fb903c828db"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98830", "GHSA-m222-4jcj-v2hx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d03c5db-e09d-3442-abd5-a7f9cbeff02d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "12df84bd-34b4-3b5e-887d-2f8f882f0d03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f95a29d40782f4f0052a692a822de3ba044b19ff <71d140099165de03128c00dd129f1eab21c6a3c4"}, {"id": "21d4823a-ed28-3c9e-b0cd-77657a0e4014", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f95a29d40782f4f0052a692a822de3ba044b19ff <7acb36fd60a3e7b858f12e69a919c3609b281408"}, {"id": "2b768772-e65d-3d74-9058-aeffa5d754d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "30fbb943-29b8-302f-a33d-ea